WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:02.479
Master Vamp!

00:02.480 --> 00:03.739
Yeah?

00:03.740 --> 00:07.419
Cool Express just
dropped off something big.

00:07.420 --> 00:09.279
It's finally here.

00:09.280 --> 00:10.459
What is this thing?

00:10.460 --> 00:12.419
Did you order a ton of
frozen food or something?

00:12.420 --> 00:13.749
Nope.

00:13.750 --> 00:14.930
It's a monster.

01:50.370 --> 01:51.529
This is a <i>monster?</i>

01:51.530 --> 01:54.599
Delz hasn't evolved
into his "perfect form" yet,

01:54.600 --> 01:57.710
so I had him packaged at low
temperatures and delivered over to us.

01:57.860 --> 02:01.009
I guess we'll have to make do like this
until he develops into his "perfect form."

02:01.010 --> 02:03.969
How are we going to take showers tonight?

02:03.970 --> 02:07.279
Why don't we all go to
the public baths together?

02:07.280 --> 02:10.190
By the way, what does
this Delz guy usually eat?

02:14.430 --> 02:16.019
Oh dear.

02:16.020 --> 02:18.119
I hadn't thought about
what to feed him at all.

02:18.120 --> 02:21.140
Let's hope he's not too
finicky about his food.

02:21.970 --> 02:24.470
Uh huh, okay.

02:24.890 --> 02:26.689
Oh I see.

02:26.690 --> 02:28.009
Yes, that's a big help.

02:28.010 --> 02:30.189
Thank you!

02:30.190 --> 02:32.119
Apparently, it eats any type of raw meat.

02:32.120 --> 02:34.239
Beef, pork, and chicken are all fine.

02:34.240 --> 02:36.909
Oh, but we don't have any
meat left over right now, do we?

02:36.910 --> 02:41.030
We still have the minced meat from the salisbury
steak we made the other day in the freezer.

02:41.230 --> 02:43.009
Minced meat would be a pain to eat, though.

02:43.010 --> 02:46.270
It'd get all messy once
it's dropped into the water.

02:46.590 --> 02:47.909
In that case,

02:47.910 --> 02:51.190
why don't we go for an early grocery
shopping trip on our way back from the baths?

02:52.830 --> 02:56.429
I guess bathing in a big tub can be a
refreshing change from time to time.

02:56.430 --> 02:59.280
My legs feel so free and relaxed right now.

03:01.470 --> 03:03.049
This is heaven.

03:03.050 --> 03:06.149
Is that Delz monster really that strong?

03:06.150 --> 03:09.449
Rumors have it that he's
something out of this world.

03:09.450 --> 03:10.410
Rumors, huh?

03:10.411 --> 03:14.209
I actually haven't seen
his true form yet either.

03:14.210 --> 03:16.569
Watching Delz in his "perfect form" should
be something to look forward to, then.

03:16.570 --> 03:18.270
Yeah.

03:19.950 --> 03:22.789
That takes care of the bath
problem and the shopping.

03:22.790 --> 03:26.259
I still can't believe we only
paid 48 cents for 100g of chicken.

03:26.260 --> 03:28.459
Is that supposed to be cheap?

03:28.460 --> 03:30.469
It may be imported meat,

03:30.470 --> 03:34.350
but this kind of price is hard to come
across even at the end of the year sales.

03:36.180 --> 03:37.349
That red necklace...

03:37.350 --> 03:39.799
that must be Mrs. Morisue's
little Mii from across the street.

03:39.800 --> 03:43.440
I guess it likes to run
around quite freely.

03:44.920 --> 03:46.689
Mii!

03:46.690 --> 03:49.149
Where did you go?

03:49.150 --> 03:51.559
Mrs. Morisue.

03:51.560 --> 03:53.199
Are you looking for little Mii?

03:53.200 --> 03:54.679
Oh, Vamp.

03:54.680 --> 03:57.459
Yes, she's disappeared. She
always used to be home at dinner time.

03:57.460 --> 04:00.379
We just saw little Mii over
by the third block just now.

04:00.380 --> 04:01.459
Really?

04:01.460 --> 04:02.819
I'm going to take a look.

04:02.820 --> 04:06.750
We'll hold on to her if she
comes back while you're gone.

04:11.470 --> 04:13.030
He's gone.

04:14.180 --> 04:19.120
He must have developed into his
"perfect form" while we were out.

04:19.670 --> 04:21.149
Master Vamp!

04:21.150 --> 04:22.890
Come quickly!

04:24.660 --> 04:28.199
I hear something
rumbling above the ceiling.

04:28.200 --> 04:30.110
That ceiling panel over there's broken!

04:30.510 --> 04:32.079
Could it be...

04:32.080 --> 04:33.080
Delz?

04:35.980 --> 04:37.670
Why did it just get quiet?

04:45.410 --> 04:47.989
Mii!

04:47.990 --> 04:48.990
From that day forward,

04:48.991 --> 04:50.959
the mysterious monster known as "Delz,"

04:50.960 --> 04:53.589
took up residence above the ceiling
of the Florsheim office in Kawasaki.

04:53.590 --> 04:55.869
What exactly is Delz?

04:55.870 --> 04:56.720
What are its intentions?

04:56.721 --> 04:59.130
And what has become of little Mii?

05:08.930 --> 05:10.319
Don't be fooled.

05:10.320 --> 05:12.989
Something being less
sweet might sound healthy,

05:12.990 --> 05:16.270
but the fact that something contains less
sugar doesn't isn't always a good thing.

05:17.300 --> 05:18.530
Sure.

05:25.330 --> 05:27.569
Vamp's Quick Recipes!

05:27.570 --> 05:29.389
Hey guys, Vamp here.

05:29.390 --> 05:31.219
You're watching our third episode.

05:31.220 --> 05:33.729
Now let's get cooking!

05:33.730 --> 05:35.439
Getting right down to business,

05:35.440 --> 05:39.080
I'll be showing you how to cook
a simple Kamatama Udon today.

05:39.380 --> 05:41.889
Here are your ingredients:

05:41.890 --> 05:44.409
First, you need a pack of
refrigerated Udon noodles,

05:44.410 --> 05:46.079
a raw egg,

05:46.080 --> 05:47.519
a pack of katsuobushi,

05:47.520 --> 05:48.629
some soy sauce,

05:48.630 --> 05:51.010
and a spring onion.

05:51.570 --> 05:53.389
Once you have these
ingredients, you're set to cook.

05:53.390 --> 05:57.829
Thaw the frozen Udon in
water and put it into a bowl,

05:57.830 --> 06:01.120
and heat it up in the microwave
until it's completely warm.

06:01.490 --> 06:06.079
Throw in the sliced spring onions,
katsuobushi, and the raw egg,

06:06.080 --> 06:08.610
add some soy sauce for flavor,

06:09.850 --> 06:12.249
and voila, the Kamatama Udon is ready.

06:12.250 --> 06:14.339
You don't have to prepare any
kind of soup for it, so it's all easy.

06:14.340 --> 06:17.099
Be sure to mix it well
and serve while still hot.

06:17.100 --> 06:19.539
This is pretty good, Master Vamp!

06:19.540 --> 06:23.049
This recipe is actually quite popular with the
folks over at Sanuki, which is the home of Udon.

06:23.050 --> 06:26.390
Frozen Udon noodles nowadays
taste really good, don't they?

06:34.590 --> 06:35.590
Welcome!

06:38.170 --> 06:39.170
A monster.

06:43.060 --> 06:44.060
What would you like?

06:45.830 --> 06:47.389
How about... a ramen.

06:47.390 --> 06:49.090
One bowl of ramen, coming up!

06:50.750 --> 06:53.360
I guess he's not a part of Florsheim.

06:53.860 --> 06:55.749
I've never seen him before.

06:55.750 --> 06:58.940
Do you work over at Vamp's by any chance?

07:00.030 --> 07:01.649
Actually, yeah.

07:01.650 --> 07:04.070
Were you a part of
Florsheim too at some point?

07:05.230 --> 07:07.109
Not really.

07:07.110 --> 07:09.409
I was more of a lone wolf.

07:09.410 --> 07:12.919
I left Shimane thinking that
I'd conquer the world by myself.

07:12.920 --> 07:15.929
Back then I really
wasn't scared of anything.

07:15.930 --> 07:19.539
I never lost to any of my
monster buddies back at home,

07:19.540 --> 07:20.410
thanks to my Drill Arrow.

07:20.411 --> 07:21.529
Drill Arrow?

07:21.530 --> 07:25.389
You put your hands together like this
and thrust the enemy while spinning around.

07:25.390 --> 07:26.819
I came up with it all by myself.

07:26.820 --> 07:28.119
Oh, for real?

07:28.120 --> 07:31.269
I used to be able to drill through
rocks 10m thick when I was in shape.

07:31.270 --> 07:32.729
For real? That's badass.

07:32.730 --> 07:34.790
Isn't it awesome?

07:37.000 --> 07:40.899
I guess I still do it once in a while when
I'm cutting through pig bones while I'm drunk.

07:40.900 --> 07:43.189
Only once in a while though.

07:43.190 --> 07:44.110
You're drunk, aren't you.

07:44.110 --> 07:44.950
Nah, I'm not drunk.

07:44.950 --> 07:45.610
Are you okay?

07:45.610 --> 07:46.610
Yeah, I'm good.

07:47.010 --> 07:50.140
So I came to Kawasaki with
that killer attack at my disposal.

07:50.440 --> 07:53.359
I probably could have planned
things better, now that I think about it.

07:53.360 --> 07:55.729
I thought I would conquer
the world someday,

07:55.730 --> 07:58.530
if I just defeated all
the heroes I ran into.

08:00.410 --> 08:03.090
And the first guy I ran into was...

08:28.640 --> 08:31.099
I think I get the basic picture.

08:31.100 --> 08:32.680
Boy was I young.

08:34.690 --> 08:36.639
That hurt my back, you punk!

08:36.640 --> 08:40.880
That was the first time
I feared for my very life.

08:43.700 --> 08:48.090
And as my consciousness faded away,

08:49.690 --> 08:54.650
I heard the sound of
my heart falling apart.

08:59.100 --> 09:00.840
You over there,

09:01.240 --> 09:02.509
are you okay?

09:02.510 --> 09:06.530
Vamp was the one who came to my rescue.

09:09.100 --> 09:11.329
There, there, it's nothing to worry about.

09:11.330 --> 09:13.639
You just chose the wrong guy to fight.

09:13.640 --> 09:15.609
That guy who beat you was Mr. Red;

09:15.610 --> 09:17.200
He's our mortal enemy.

09:17.600 --> 09:21.109
But you sure are brave, aren't you, Horai?

09:21.110 --> 09:22.749
Youth sure is a wonderful thing.

09:22.750 --> 09:25.640
I was reckless when I
was around your age too.

09:26.140 --> 09:30.860
Here, you should drink something
warm and rest on your side for a while.

09:31.750 --> 09:34.749
We're going to fight Mr. Red tomorrow too.

09:34.750 --> 09:37.840
Don't worry, we'll avenge you.

09:38.240 --> 09:41.490
So what happened the next day?

09:42.800 --> 09:46.360
Oh, they got the beating of their lives.

09:46.960 --> 09:48.939
Are you okay there, Guzley?

09:48.940 --> 09:50.519
Try lying down for a bit.

09:50.520 --> 09:52.169
It hurts so bad.

09:52.170 --> 09:53.829
I'm so sorry.

09:53.830 --> 09:57.189
Red was apparently really pissed
because he thought I was part of Florsheim,

09:57.190 --> 09:59.986
and that would mean that Florsheim was
trying to catch him with his pants down.

10:00.010 --> 10:01.129
With his pants down, eh?

10:01.130 --> 10:02.130
You heard me.

10:03.690 --> 10:05.649
I think maybe three of
your ribs are cracked.

10:05.650 --> 10:07.219
Is your head okay?

10:07.220 --> 10:08.969
He kinda kicked it
around like a soccer ball.

10:08.970 --> 10:10.849
Y-Yeah.

10:10.850 --> 10:12.339
You don't have to worry about me.

10:12.340 --> 10:14.209
What about you, Master Vamp?

10:14.210 --> 10:16.580
Is your back all right?

10:16.930 --> 10:18.829
No worries.

10:18.830 --> 10:21.219
I was just overreacting.

10:21.220 --> 10:24.869
But Red was kicking
you all over the place...

10:24.870 --> 10:26.299
I said it's fine.

10:26.300 --> 10:27.909
I'm used to it already.

10:27.910 --> 10:29.999
You're <i>used</i> to it?

10:30.000 --> 10:33.000
So you guys have been
fighting that red thing all this time?

10:33.700 --> 10:34.719
That's right.

10:34.720 --> 10:39.030
Mr. Red isn't our fated
rival for nothing, you know.

10:39.670 --> 10:41.419
Seconds, please.

10:41.420 --> 10:42.819
That's great.

10:42.820 --> 10:45.519
Having that kind of appetite
must mean you're getting better.

10:45.520 --> 10:49.190
Let's eat well so that we can
put an end to Mr. Red next time!

10:51.670 --> 10:54.499
That reminds me, I saw a
celebrity over at Nikotama yesterday.

10:54.500 --> 10:55.410
Really? Who was it?

10:55.411 --> 10:57.389
There was Red, who
was as strong as a demon,

10:57.390 --> 10:59.790
and Vamp, who had the heart of a champion.

11:00.890 --> 11:07.450
Seeing those two made me realize that someone
like me isn't cut out to conquer the world.

11:10.190 --> 11:11.789
Here you go.

11:11.790 --> 11:15.799
I found work at a ramen house after that,

11:15.800 --> 11:19.480
and before I knew it, I
ended up with my own shop.

11:23.650 --> 11:27.169
Have you ever regretted
giving up world domination?

11:27.170 --> 11:28.720
Never.

11:29.570 --> 11:32.379
Business has been good for me.

11:32.380 --> 11:34.490
I've even got a few loyal customers.

11:40.400 --> 11:41.400
Welcome!

11:41.720 --> 11:42.630
I'll take the usual.

11:42.631 --> 11:44.270
Me too.

11:44.670 --> 11:47.290
Mr. Red! Kayoko!

11:47.830 --> 11:48.859
Over here!

11:48.860 --> 11:50.510
Vamp!

11:50.910 --> 11:52.689
I didn't know you were here.

11:52.690 --> 11:55.119
The ramen here is really good.

11:55.120 --> 11:56.909
Why are you coming over here?

11:56.910 --> 11:58.189
Why not?

11:58.190 --> 11:59.519
Let's all eat together.

11:59.520 --> 12:00.420
Yeah.

12:00.421 --> 12:02.570
And here you go, two Menma Ramen bowls.

12:04.630 --> 12:06.759
The food here never gets better does it.

12:06.760 --> 12:08.009
Come on...

12:08.010 --> 12:09.769
You really should stop complaining.

12:09.770 --> 12:11.609
Yeah, the ramen's actually really good.

12:11.610 --> 12:12.360
Thank you!

12:12.361 --> 12:13.839
Astro Fighter Sunred.

12:13.840 --> 12:16.169
This is the story about the
conflict between good and evil

12:16.170 --> 12:18.730
which takes place in the city of Kawasaki.
